IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026): part sga1, module 3.
-- Part 4, Division 3 (shares): ss 62A to 63C: no par value shares, the transitional provisions for s 62A, and the returns and lodgments that follow an allotment.
--
-- Every function answers MAYBE (BOOLEAN, NUMBER ...): JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words, NOTHING is "the text does not say".
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. NOTES.md ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sga1)") has the rule of 2026-10-29 and the two readings "for a lawyer".
-- A duty with a time limit is asked as a "late" function: JUST TRUE means the duty was not done in time. "Within N days after X" is counted by the keel's
-- `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after`: an act on the day of X itself is in time (an early act is in time; fork F-X3 in NOTES.md).

§ `Section 62A: no par value shares`

-- 62A.-(1) Shares of a company have no par or nominal value.
-- src:6334 | 62A.—(1) Shares of a company have no par or nominal value.
@ref s 62A(1) (src:6334)
GIVEN `the thing is a share of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62A(1) the share has a par or nominal value` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a share of a company`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Shares of a company have no par or nominal value"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Shares of a company" -- a thing that is not a share of a company is not covered

-- (2) Subsection (1) applies to all shares, whether issued before, on or after 30 January 2006.
-- src:6336 | (2) Subsection (1) applies to all shares, whether issued before, on or
-- src:6337 | after 30 January 2006.
@ref s 62A(2) (src:6336-6337)
GIVEN `the day the share was issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62A(2) subsection (1) applies to the share` MEANS
    JUST TRUE   -- the text says "all shares, whether issued before, on or after 30 January 2006": every issue date is covered, so no date gives a "no"

§ `Section 62B: transitional provisions for section 62A`

-- The date the section works from.
-- src:6341 | 62B.—(1) For the purpose of the operation of this Act on or after
-- src:6342 | 30 January 2006 in relation to a share issued before that date —
@ref s 62B(1) (src:6341-6342)
`s 62B the day 30 January 2006` MEANS Date 30 1 2006

-- (1) For the operation of the Act on or after 30 January 2006 in relation to a share issued before that date: (a) the amount paid on the share is the sum of all amounts paid to the company at any
-- time for the share (not including any premium); and (b) the amount unpaid is the difference between the price of issue (not including any premium) and the amount paid.
-- src:6341 | 62B.—(1) For the purpose of the operation of this Act on or after
-- src:6342 | 30 January 2006 in relation to a share issued before that date —
-- src:6344 | (a) the amount paid on the share is the sum of all amounts paid
-- src:6345 | to the company at any time for the share (but not including
-- src:6346 | any premium); and
@ref s 62B(1)(a) (src:6341-6346)
GIVEN `the share was issued before 30 January 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amounts paid to the company at any time for the share, not including any premium, in Singapore dollars` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 62B(1)(a) the amount paid on the share` MEANS
    IF `the share was issued before 30 January 2006`
    THEN JUST (sum `the amounts paid to the company at any time for the share, not including any premium, in Singapore dollars`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to a share issued before that date" -- a share issued on or after 30 January 2006 is not covered

-- (b) the amount unpaid on the share is the difference between the price of issue of the share (not including any premium) and the amount paid on the share.
-- src:6348 | (b) the amount unpaid on the share is the difference between
-- src:6349 | the price of issue of the share (but not including any
-- src:6350 | premium) and the amount paid on the share.
@ref s 62B(1)(b) (src:6348-6350)
GIVEN `the share was issued before 30 January 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the price of issue of the share, not including any premium, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amounts paid to the company at any time for the share, not including any premium, in Singapore dollars` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 62B(1)(b) the amount unpaid on the share` MEANS
    IF `the share was issued before 30 January 2006`
    THEN JUST (`the price of issue of the share, not including any premium, in Singapore dollars` MINUS (sum `the amounts paid to the company at any time for the share, not including any premium, in Singapore dollars`))
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to a share issued before that date" -- a share issued on or after 30 January 2006 is not covered

-- (2) On 30 January 2006, any amount standing to the credit of a company's share premium account and any amount standing to the credit of its capital redemption reserve becomes part of the company's share capital.
-- src:6352 | (2) On 30 January 2006, any amount standing to the credit of a
-- src:6353 | company’s share premium account and any amount standing to the
-- src:6358 | credit of a company’s capital redemption reserve becomes part of the
-- src:6359 | company’s share capital.
@ref s 62B(2) (src:6352-6359)
GIVEN `the amount stood to the credit of the company's share premium account or capital redemption reserve on 30 January 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62B(2) the amount has become part of the company's share capital` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the amount stood to the credit of the company's share premium account or capital redemption reserve on 30 January 2006`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any amount standing to the credit of a company's share premium account and any amount standing to the credit of a company's capital redemption reserve" -- any other amount is not covered
    ELSE (IF `the day on which the question is asked` AT LEAST `s 62B the day 30 January 2006`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On 30 January 2006, any amount ... becomes part of the company's share capital" -- a date fixed in the text's own words, not yet reached (periods ruling (a))

-- (3) Despite (2), a company may use the amount standing to the credit of its share premium account immediately before 30 January 2006 to (a) provide for the premium payable on redemption of debentures or redeemable
-- preference shares issued before that date; (b) write off (i) the preliminary expenses incurred before that date or (ii) expenses incurred, or commissions or brokerages paid or discounts allowed, on or before that date,
-- for or on any duty, fee or tax payable on or in connection with any issue of shares; (c) pay up, pursuant to an agreement made before that date, shares unissued before that date to be issued on or after it to members as fully
-- paid bonus shares; (d) pay up in whole or in part the balance unpaid on shares issued before that date to members; or (e) pay dividends declared before that date, if satisfied by the issue of shares to members.
-- src:6361 | (3) Despite subsection (2), a company may use the amount standing
-- src:6362 | to the credit of its share premium account immediately before
-- src:6363 | 30 January 2006 to —
-- src:6365 | (a) provide for the premium payable on redemption of
-- src:6366 | debentures or redeemable preference shares issued
-- src:6367 | before that date;
-- src:6369 | (b) write off —
-- src:6371 | (i) the preliminary expenses of the company incurred
-- src:6372 | before that date; or
-- src:6374 | (ii) expenses incurred, or commissions or brokerages
-- src:6375 | paid or discounts allowed, on or before that date, for
-- src:6376 | or on any duty, fee or tax payable on or in connection
-- src:6377 | with any issue of shares of the company;
-- src:6379 | (c) pay up, pursuant to an agreement made before that date,
-- src:6380 | shares which were unissued before that date and which are
-- src:6381 | to be issued on or after that date to members of the
-- src:6382 | company as fully paid bonus shares;
-- src:6384 | (d) pay up in whole or in part the balance unpaid on shares
-- src:6385 | issued before that date to members of the company; or
-- src:6387 | (e) pay dividends declared before that date, if such dividends
-- src:6388 | are satisfied by the issue of shares to members of the
-- src:6389 | company.
@ref s 62B(3) (src:6361-6389)
DECLARE `s 62B(3) use of the share premium account` IS ONE OF
    `s 62B(3)(a) provide for the premium payable on redemption of debentures or redeemable preference shares`
        HAS `s 62B(3)(a) the debentures or redeemable preference shares were issued before 30 January 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 62B(3)(b)(i) write off the preliminary expenses of the company`
        HAS `s 62B(3)(b)(i) the preliminary expenses were incurred before 30 January 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 62B(3)(b)(ii) write off expenses, commissions, brokerages or discounts on a duty, fee or tax on an issue of shares`
        HAS `s 62B(3)(b)(ii) the expenses were incurred, or the commissions or brokerages paid or discounts allowed, on or before 30 January 2006 for or on a duty, fee or tax payable on or in connection with an issue of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 62B(3)(c) pay up shares as fully paid bonus shares to members`
        HAS `s 62B(3)(c) the shares are paid up pursuant to an agreement made before 30 January 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
            `s 62B(3)(c) the shares were unissued before 30 January 2006 and are to be issued on or after that date to members as fully paid bonus shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 62B(3)(d) pay up the balance unpaid on shares issued to members`
        HAS `s 62B(3)(d) the shares were issued before 30 January 2006 to members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 62B(3)(e) pay dividends satisfied by the issue of shares to members`
        HAS `s 62B(3)(e) the dividends were declared before 30 January 2006 and are satisfied by the issue of shares to members` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 62B(3) some other use`

@ref s 62B(3) (src:6361-6389)
GIVEN `the amount stood to the credit of the company's share premium account immediately before 30 January 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
      use IS A `s 62B(3) use of the share premium account`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62B(3) the company may use the amount for the purpose` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the amount stood to the credit of the company's share premium account immediately before 30 January 2006`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the amount standing to the credit of its share premium account immediately before 30 January 2006" -- another amount is not covered (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1: fork line in NOTES.md)
    ELSE CONSIDER use
         WHEN `s 62B(3)(a) provide for the premium payable on redemption of debentures or redeemable preference shares` before THEN
             (IF before THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "debentures or redeemable preference shares issued before that date" -- others are not covered (grant ruling, limit 1)
         WHEN `s 62B(3)(b)(i) write off the preliminary expenses of the company` before THEN
             (IF before THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the preliminary expenses of the company incurred before that date" -- others are not covered (grant ruling, limit 1)
         WHEN `s 62B(3)(b)(ii) write off expenses, commissions, brokerages or discounts on a duty, fee or tax on an issue of shares` onOrBefore THEN
             (IF onOrBefore THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "expenses incurred, or commissions or brokerages paid or discounts allowed, on or before that date" -- others are not covered (grant ruling, limit 1)
         WHEN `s 62B(3)(c) pay up shares as fully paid bonus shares to members` agreed unissued THEN
             (IF agreed AND unissued THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "pursuant to an agreement made before that date, shares which were unissued before that date and which are to be issued on or after that date to members of the company as fully paid bonus shares" -- others are not covered (grant ruling, limit 1)
         WHEN `s 62B(3)(d) pay up the balance unpaid on shares issued to members` issuedBefore THEN
             (IF issuedBefore THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the balance unpaid on shares issued before that date to members of the company" -- others are not covered (grant ruling, limit 1)
         WHEN `s 62B(3)(e) pay dividends satisfied by the issue of shares to members` declared THEN
             (IF declared THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "dividends declared before that date, if such dividends are satisfied by the issue of shares to members of the company" -- others are not covered (grant ruling, limit 1)
         WHEN `s 62B(3) some other use` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraphs (a) to (e) are listed without "only", and the subsection says nothing of any other use

-- (4) Despite (2), if the company carries on insurance business in Singapore immediately before 30 January 2006, it may also apply the amount standing to the credit of its share premium account immediately before
-- that date by appropriation or transfer to any fund established and maintained pursuant to the Insurance Act 1966.
-- src:6391 | (4) Despite subsection (2), if the company carries on insurance
-- src:6392 | business in Singapore immediately before 30 January 2006, it may
-- src:6393 | also apply the amount standing to the credit of its share premium
-- src:6394 | account immediately before that date by appropriation or transfer to
-- src:6395 | any fund established and maintained pursuant to the Insurance
-- src:6396 | Act 1966.
@ref s 62B(4) (src:6391-6396)
GIVEN `the company carried on insurance business in Singapore immediately before 30 January 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount is applied by appropriation or transfer to a fund established and maintained pursuant to the Insurance Act 1966` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62B(4) the insurance company may also apply the amount to a fund under the Insurance Act 1966` MEANS
    IF `the company carried on insurance business in Singapore immediately before 30 January 2006` AND `the amount is applied by appropriation or transfer to a fund established and maintained pursuant to the Insurance Act 1966`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the company carries on insurance business in Singapore immediately before 30 January 2006, it may also apply the amount ... by appropriation or transfer to any fund established and maintained pursuant to the Insurance Act 1966" -- a grant whose "if" gate or named complement is unmet (grant ruling, limit 1: fork line in NOTES.md)

-- (5) Despite (1), the liability of a shareholder for calls in respect of money unpaid on shares issued before 30 January 2006 (whether on account of the par value of the shares or by way of premium)
-- is not affected by the shares ceasing to have a par value.
-- src:6398 | (5) Despite subsection (1), the liability of a shareholder for calls in
-- src:6399 | respect of money unpaid on shares issued before 30 January 2006
-- src:6400 | (whether on account of the par value of the shares or by way of
-- src:6401 | premium) is not affected by the shares ceasing to have a par value.
@ref s 62B(5) (src:6398-6401)
GIVEN `the shares were issued before 30 January 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62B(5) the shareholder's liability for calls on the unpaid money is affected by the shares ceasing to have a par value` MEANS
    IF `the shares were issued before 30 January 2006`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the liability of a shareholder for calls in respect of money unpaid on shares issued before 30 January 2006 (whether on account of the par value of the shares or by way of premium) is not affected by the shares ceasing to have a par value"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shares issued before 30 January 2006" -- shares issued on or after it are not covered

-- (6) For interpreting and applying, on or after 30 January 2006, a contract (including the constitution) entered into before that date or a trust deed or other document executed before that date: (a) a reference to
-- the par or nominal value of a share is a reference to (i) if the share is issued before that date, the par or nominal value immediately before that date; (ii) if issued on or after that date but shares of the same class
-- were on issue immediately before it, the value the share would have had if issued then; or (iii) if issued on or after that date and shares of the same class were not on issue immediately before it, the value determined
-- by the directors; and a reference to share premium is a reference to any residual share capital in relation to the share; (b) a reference to a right to a return of capital on a share is a reference to a right to a return of capital
-- of a value equal to the amount paid in respect of the share's par or nominal value; and (c) a reference to the aggregate par or nominal value of the company's issued share capital is a reference to that aggregate as it existed
-- immediately before that date, increased for the par or nominal value (as in (a)) of shares issued on or after that date and reduced for that of shares cancelled on or after that date.
-- src:6406 | (6) For the purpose of interpreting and applying, on or after
-- src:6407 | 30 January 2006, a contract (including the constitution of the
-- src:6408 | company) entered into before that date or a trust deed or other
-- src:6409 | document executed before that date —
-- src:6411 | (a) a reference to the par or nominal value of a share is a
-- src:6412 | reference to —
-- src:6414 | (i) if the share is issued before that date — the par or
-- src:6415 | nominal value of the share immediately before that
-- src:6416 | date;
-- src:6418 | (ii) if the share is issued on or after that date but shares of
-- src:6419 | the same class were on issue immediately before that
-- src:6420 | date — the par or nominal value that the share would
-- src:6421 | have had if it had been issued then; or
-- src:6423 | (iii) if the share is issued on or after that date and shares
-- src:6424 | of the same class were not on issue immediately
-- src:6425 | before that date — the par or nominal value
-- src:6426 | determined by the directors,
-- src:6428 | (a) and a reference to share premium is a reference to any
-- src:6429 | residual share capital in relation to the share;
-- src:6431 | (b) a reference to a right to a return of capital on a share is a
-- src:6432 | reference to a right to a return of capital of a value equal to
-- src:6433 | the amount paid in respect of the share’s par or nominal
-- src:6434 | value; and
-- src:6436 | (c) a reference to the aggregate par or nominal value of the
-- src:6437 | company’s issued share capital is a reference to that
-- src:6438 | aggregate as it existed immediately before that date as —
-- src:6440 | (i) increased to take account of the par or nominal value
-- src:6441 | as defined in paragraph (a) of any shares issued on or
-- src:6442 | after that date; and
-- src:6444 | (ii) reduced to take account of the par or nominal value
-- src:6445 | as defined in paragraph (a) of any shares cancelled
-- src:6446 | on or after that date.
@ref s 62B(6) (src:6406-6446)
DECLARE `s 62B(6)(a) when the share was issued` IS ONE OF
    `s 62B(6)(a)(i) the share is issued before 30 January 2006`
    `s 62B(6)(a)(ii) the share is issued on or after 30 January 2006 and shares of the same class were on issue immediately before that date`
    `s 62B(6)(a)(iii) the share is issued on or after 30 January 2006 and shares of the same class were not on issue immediately before that date`

@ref s 62B(6)(a) (src:6406-6426)
GIVEN `the document was entered into or executed before 30 January 2006 and is being interpreted or applied on or after that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      issue IS A `s 62B(6)(a) when the share was issued`
      `the par or nominal value of the share immediately before 30 January 2006, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the par or nominal value the share would have had if it had been issued immediately before 30 January 2006, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the par or nominal value determined by the directors, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 62B(6)(a) the par or nominal value to which the reference in the document refers` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the document was entered into or executed before 30 January 2006 and is being interpreted or applied on or after that date`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purpose of interpreting and applying, on or after 30 January 2006, a contract ... entered into before that date or a trust deed or other document executed before that date" -- another document is not covered
    ELSE CONSIDER issue
         WHEN `s 62B(6)(a)(i) the share is issued before 30 January 2006` THEN JUST `the par or nominal value of the share immediately before 30 January 2006, in Singapore dollars`
         WHEN `s 62B(6)(a)(ii) the share is issued on or after 30 January 2006 and shares of the same class were on issue immediately before that date` THEN JUST `the par or nominal value the share would have had if it had been issued immediately before 30 January 2006, in Singapore dollars`
         WHEN `s 62B(6)(a)(iii) the share is issued on or after 30 January 2006 and shares of the same class were not on issue immediately before that date` THEN JUST `the par or nominal value determined by the directors, in Singapore dollars`

@ref s 62B(6)(a) (src:6406-6429)
GIVEN `the document was entered into or executed before 30 January 2006 and is being interpreted or applied on or after that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the residual share capital in relation to the share, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 62B(6)(a) the share premium to which the reference in the document refers` MEANS
    IF `the document was entered into or executed before 30 January 2006 and is being interpreted or applied on or after that date`
    THEN JUST `the residual share capital in relation to the share, in Singapore dollars`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purpose of interpreting and applying, on or after 30 January 2006, a contract ... entered into before that date" -- another document is not covered

@ref s 62B(6)(b) (src:6431-6434)
GIVEN `the document was entered into or executed before 30 January 2006 and is being interpreted or applied on or after that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount paid in respect of the share's par or nominal value, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 62B(6)(b) the value of the right to a return of capital on the share to which the reference in the document refers` MEANS
    IF `the document was entered into or executed before 30 January 2006 and is being interpreted or applied on or after that date`
    THEN JUST `the amount paid in respect of the share's par or nominal value, in Singapore dollars`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purpose of interpreting and applying, on or after 30 January 2006, a contract ... entered into before that date" -- another document is not covered

@ref s 62B(6)(c) (src:6436-6446)
GIVEN `the document was entered into or executed before 30 January 2006 and is being interpreted or applied on or after that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggregate par or nominal value of the company's issued share capital as it existed immediately before 30 January 2006, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the par or nominal value, as defined in paragraph (a), of the shares issued on or after 30 January 2006, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the par or nominal value, as defined in paragraph (a), of the shares cancelled on or after 30 January 2006, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 62B(6)(c) the aggregate par or nominal value of the company's issued share capital to which the reference in the document refers` MEANS
    IF `the document was entered into or executed before 30 January 2006 and is being interpreted or applied on or after that date`
    THEN JUST ((`the aggregate par or nominal value of the company's issued share capital as it existed immediately before 30 January 2006, in Singapore dollars` PLUS `the par or nominal value, as defined in paragraph (a), of the shares issued on or after 30 January 2006, in Singapore dollars`) MINUS `the par or nominal value, as defined in paragraph (a), of the shares cancelled on or after 30 January 2006, in Singapore dollars`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purpose of interpreting and applying, on or after 30 January 2006, a contract ... entered into before that date" -- another document is not covered

-- (7) A company may (a) at any time before (i) the date it is required under section 197(4) in force immediately before 3 January 2016 to lodge its first annual return after 30 January 2006, or (ii) the expiry of
-- 6 months from 30 January 2006, whichever is the earlier; or (b) within such longer period as the Registrar may, if he or she thinks fit in the circumstances of the case, allow, file with the Registrar a notice in the
-- prescribed form of its share capital. A date the text fixes (the earlier of (i) and (ii)) or a longer period the Registrar allowed: outside both, the answer is JUST FALSE (periods ruling (a)); fork F-IS2.
-- src:6453 | (7) A company may —
-- src:6455 | (a) at any time before —
-- src:6457 | (i) the date it is required under section 197(4) in force
-- src:6458 | immediately before 3 January 2016 to lodge its first
-- src:6459 | annual return after 30 January 2006; or
-- src:6461 | (ii) the expiry of 6 months from 30 January 2006,
-- src:6463 | (a) whichever is the earlier; or
-- src:6465 | (b) within such longer period as the Registrar may, if he or she
-- src:6466 | thinks fit in the circumstances of the case, allow,
-- src:6468 | file with the Registrar a notice in the prescribed form of its share
-- src:6469 | capital.
@ref s 62B(7) (src:6453-6469)
GIVEN `the day the notice of the company's share capital is filed` IS A DATE
      `the date the company was required under section 197(4) in force immediately before 3 January 2016 to lodge its first annual return after 30 January 2006` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the longer period the Registrar allowed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62B(7) the company may file the notice of its share capital` MEANS
    IF    (    `the day the notice of the company's share capital is filed` LESS THAN `the date the company was required under section 197(4) in force immediately before 3 January 2016 to lodge its first annual return after 30 January 2006`
           AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `s 62B the day 30 January 2006` `the day the notice of the company's share capital is filed` 6 Months)
       OR (    `the Registrar allowed a longer period`
           AND `the day the notice of the company's share capital is filed` AT MOST `the last day of the longer period the Registrar allowed`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time before ... whichever is the earlier; or ... within such longer period as the Registrar may ... allow" -- both periods the text fixes have gone (periods ruling (a); fork F-IS2)

-- (8) Unless a company has filed a notice of its share capital under (7), the Registrar may for the purposes of the records maintained by the Authority adopt, as the share capital of the company, the aggregate nominal
-- value of the shares issued by the company as that value appears in the Authority's records immediately before 30 January 2006.
-- src:6473 | (8) Unless a company has filed a notice of its share capital under
-- src:6474 | subsection (7), the Registrar may for the purposes of the records
-- src:6475 | maintained by the Authority adopt, as the share capital of the
-- src:6476 | company, the aggregate nominal value of the shares issued by the
-- src:6477 | company as that value appears in the Authority’s records immediately
-- src:6478 | before 30 January 2006.
@ref s 62B(8) (src:6473-6478)
GIVEN `the company has filed a notice of its share capital under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62B(8) the Registrar may adopt the aggregate nominal value in the Authority's records as the company's share capital` MEANS
    IF `the company has filed a notice of its share capital under subsection (7)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless a company has filed a notice of its share capital under subsection (7), the Registrar may ... adopt" -- an "unless" gate that closes the grant (grant ruling, limit 2; fork line in NOTES.md)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 62B(8) (src:6473-6478)
GIVEN `the company has filed a notice of its share capital under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggregate nominal value of the shares issued by the company as it appears in the Authority's records immediately before 30 January 2006, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 62B(8) the share capital the Registrar may adopt for the Authority's records` MEANS
    IF `the company has filed a notice of its share capital under subsection (7)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless a company has filed a notice of its share capital under subsection (7)" -- the subsection says nothing of a company that has filed
    ELSE JUST `the aggregate nominal value of the shares issued by the company as it appears in the Authority's records immediately before 30 January 2006, in Singapore dollars`

§ `Section 63: return as to allotments by private companies`

-- 63.-(1) A private company may allot new shares, other than a deemed allotment, by lodging with the Registrar a return of the allotment in the prescribed form.
-- A grant ("may ... by lodging"): where the return is not lodged the answer is NOTHING, not "may not" (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line in NOTES.md).
-- src:6482 | 63.—(1) A private company may allot new shares, other than a
-- src:6483 | deemed allotment, by lodging with the Registrar a return of the
-- src:6484 | allotment in the prescribed form, which must include the following
-- src:6485 | particulars:
@ref s 63(1) (src:6482-6485)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allotment is a deemed allotment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a return of the allotment in the prescribed form has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63(1) the private company may allot the new shares by lodging the return` MEANS
    IF    `the company is a private company`
      AND (NOT `the allotment is a deemed allotment`)
      AND `a return of the allotment in the prescribed form has been lodged with the Registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private company may allot new shares, other than a deemed allotment, by lodging with the Registrar a return of the allotment in the prescribed form" -- a grant whose gate is unmet (grant ruling, limit 1)

-- The particulars the return must include: (a) the number of shares; (b) the amount (if any) paid or deemed to be paid on each; (c) the amount (if any) unpaid on each; (d) where the capital is divided into shares of different classes,
-- the class of each share; (e) for each member: (i) the full name; (ii) the identification and nationality, if required by the Registrar; (iii) the residential address and contact address (if an individual) or the address (if otherwise);
-- (iv) the number and class of shares held.
-- src:6487 | (a) the number of the shares comprised in the allotment;
-- src:6489 | (b) the amount (if any) paid or deemed to be paid on the
-- src:6490 | allotment of each share;
-- src:6492 | (c) the amount (if any) unpaid on each share referred to in
-- src:6493 | paragraph (b);
-- src:6495 | (d) where the capital of the company is divided into shares of
-- src:6496 | different classes, the class of shares to which each share
-- src:6497 | comprised in the allotment belongs; and
-- src:6502 | (e) for each member of the private company —
-- src:6504 | (i) the full name;
-- src:6506 | (ii) the identification and nationality, if required by the
-- src:6507 | Registrar;
-- src:6509 | (iii) the residential address and contact address (if the
-- src:6510 | member is an individual) or the address (if
-- src:6511 | otherwise); and
-- src:6513 | (iv) the number and class of shares held.
@ref s 63(1) (src:6487-6513)
GIVEN `the return states the number of the shares comprised in the allotment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return states the amount, if any, paid or deemed to be paid on the allotment of each share` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return states the amount, if any, unpaid on each share` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the capital of the company is divided into shares of different classes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return states the class of shares to which each share comprised in the allotment belongs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return states the full name of each member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar requires the identification and nationality` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return states the identification and nationality of each member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return states the residential address and the contact address of each member who is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return states the address of each member who is not an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return states the number and class of shares held by each member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63(1) the return includes the particulars the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the return states the number of the shares comprised in the allotment`
      AND `the return states the amount, if any, paid or deemed to be paid on the allotment of each share`
      AND `the return states the amount, if any, unpaid on each share`
      AND ((NOT `the capital of the company is divided into shares of different classes`) OR `the return states the class of shares to which each share comprised in the allotment belongs`)
      AND `the return states the full name of each member`
      AND ((NOT `the Registrar requires the identification and nationality`) OR `the return states the identification and nationality of each member`)
      AND `the return states the residential address and the contact address of each member who is an individual`
      AND `the return states the address of each member who is not an individual`
      AND `the return states the number and class of shares held by each member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a return of the allotment in the prescribed form, which must include the following particulars: (a) the number of the shares comprised in the allotment; (b) the amount (if any) paid or deemed to be paid on the allotment of each share; (c) the amount (if any) unpaid on each share ...; (d) where the capital of the company is divided into shares of different classes, the class of shares ...; and (e) for each member of the private company" (a duty not met, the subsection's own question)

-- (2) An allotment of shares, other than a deemed allotment, by a private company on or after 3 January 2016 does not take effect until the electronic register of members of the company is updated by the Registrar
-- under section 196A(5). The "until" bar (delegated-definitions ruling (d)): JUST TRUE until the register is updated, JUST FALSE after. A public company, a deemed allotment or an earlier allotment is not covered.
-- src:6519 | (2) An allotment of shares, other than a deemed allotment, by a
-- src:6520 | private company on or after 3 January 2016 does not take effect until
-- src:6521 | the electronic register of members of the company is updated by the
-- src:6522 | Registrar under section 196A(5).
@ref s 63(2) (src:6519-6522)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allotment is a deemed allotment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the allotment` IS A DATE
      `the electronic register of members of the company has been updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63(2) the allotment has not yet taken effect` MEANS
    IF    (NOT `the company is a private company`)
       OR `the allotment is a deemed allotment`
       OR `the day of the allotment` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An allotment of shares, other than a deemed allotment, by a private company on or after 3 January 2016" -- a public company, a deemed allotment or an allotment before 3 January 2016 is not covered (periods ruling (c): a scope limit with no "only"; fork F-X1)
    ELSE (IF `the electronic register of members of the company has been updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not take effect until the electronic register of members of the company is updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)" -- the register has been updated, so the bar is over
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (3) In this section and section 63A, "deemed allotment" means an issue of shares without formal allotment to subscribers to the constitution.
-- src:6526 | (3) In this section and section 63A, “deemed allotment” means an
-- src:6527 | issue of shares without formal allotment to subscribers to the
-- src:6528 | constitution.
@ref s 63(3) (src:6526-6528)
GIVEN `the issue of shares is made without formal allotment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issue is to subscribers to the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63(3) "deemed allotment" the issue is a deemed allotment` MEANS
    IF `the issue of shares is made without formal allotment` AND `the issue is to subscribers to the constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): ""deemed allotment" means an issue of shares without formal allotment to subscribers to the constitution" (a "means" definition)

§ `Section 63A: return as to allotments by public companies`

-- 63A.-(1) Where a public company makes any allotment of its shares, other than a deemed allotment, the company must within 14 days thereafter lodge with the Registrar a return of the allotments stating
-- (a) the number of the shares; (b) the amount (if any) paid or deemed to be paid on each; (c) the amount (if any) unpaid on each; (d) where the capital is divided into classes, the class of each share; and (e) for each of the 50 members who,
-- following the allotment, hold the most number of shares (excluding treasury shares): (i) the full name; (ii) the identification and nationality, if required by the Registrar; (iii) the residential address and contact address
-- (if an individual) or the address (if otherwise); (iv) the number and class of shares held.
-- Asked as "late": JUST TRUE where the return was lodged after the 14th day, or is still not lodged after it. The "Where" gate failing answers JUST FALSE (periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a)).
-- src:6534 | 63A.—(1) Where a public company makes any allotment of its
-- src:6535 | shares, other than a deemed allotment, the company must within
-- src:6536 | 14 days thereafter lodge with the Registrar a return of the allotments
-- src:6537 | stating —
-- src:6539 | (a) the number of the shares comprised in the allotment;
-- src:6541 | (b) the amount (if any) paid or deemed to be paid on the
-- src:6542 | allotment of each share;
-- src:6544 | (c) the amount (if any) unpaid on each share referred to in
-- src:6545 | paragraph (b);
-- src:6547 | (d) where the capital of the company is divided into shares of
-- src:6548 | different classes, the class of shares to which each share
-- src:6549 | comprised in the allotment belongs; and
-- src:6554 | (e) for each of the 50 members of the public company who,
-- src:6555 | following the allotment, hold the most number of shares in
-- src:6556 | the company (excluding treasury shares) —
-- src:6558 | (i) the full name;
-- src:6560 | (ii) the identification and nationality, if required by the
-- src:6561 | Registrar;
-- src:6563 | (iii) the residential address and contact address (if the
-- src:6564 | member is an individual) or the address (if
-- src:6565 | otherwise); and
-- src:6567 | (iv) the number and class of shares held.
@ref s 63A(1) (src:6534-6567)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allotment is a deemed allotment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the allotment` IS A DATE
      `a return of the allotment has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the return of the allotment was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63A(1) the public company is late in lodging the return of the allotment` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a public company`) OR `the allotment is a deemed allotment`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a public company makes any allotment of its shares, other than a deemed allotment, the company must within 14 days thereafter lodge" -- a failed "where" (periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a)): the duty does not arise
    ELSE (IF `a return of the allotment has been lodged with the Registrar`
          THEN (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the allotment` `the day the return of the allotment was lodged` 14 Days
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must within 14 days thereafter lodge with the Registrar a return" -- lodged within the 14 days (a period the text fixes in its own words: periods ruling (a))
                ELSE JUST TRUE)
          ELSE (IF `the day on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the allotment` 14 Days
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must within 14 days thereafter lodge" -- the 14 days have not yet run out (periods ruling (a))

@ref s 63A(1) (src:6534-6567)
GIVEN `the return states the number of the shares comprised in the allotment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return states the amount, if any, paid or deemed to be paid on the allotment of each share` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return states the amount, if any, unpaid on each share` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the capital of the company is divided into shares of different classes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return states the class of shares to which each share comprised in the allotment belongs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (2) excuses the return from stating the particulars in paragraph (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return states the full name of each of the 50 largest members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar requires the identification and nationality` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return states the identification and nationality of each of the 50 largest members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return states the residential address and the contact address of each of those members who is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return states the address of each of those members who is not an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return states the number and class of shares held by each of the 50 largest members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63A(1) the return states the particulars the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the return states the number of the shares comprised in the allotment`
      AND `the return states the amount, if any, paid or deemed to be paid on the allotment of each share`
      AND `the return states the amount, if any, unpaid on each share`
      AND ((NOT `the capital of the company is divided into shares of different classes`) OR `the return states the class of shares to which each share comprised in the allotment belongs`)
      AND (   `subsection (2) excuses the return from stating the particulars in paragraph (e)`
           OR (    `the return states the full name of each of the 50 largest members`
               AND ((NOT `the Registrar requires the identification and nationality`) OR `the return states the identification and nationality of each of the 50 largest members`)
               AND `the return states the residential address and the contact address of each of those members who is an individual`
               AND `the return states the address of each of those members who is not an individual`
               AND `the return states the number and class of shares held by each of the 50 largest members`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "lodge with the Registrar a return of the allotments stating -- (a) the number of the shares comprised in the allotment; (b) the amount (if any) paid ...; (c) the amount (if any) unpaid ...; (d) where the capital of the company is divided into shares of different classes, the class of shares ...; and (e) for each of the 50 members of the public company who, following the allotment, hold the most number of shares in the company (excluding treasury shares)" (a duty not met, the subsection's own question)

DECLARE `s 63A act` IS ONE OF
    `s 63A(1) lodge with the Registrar a return of the allotments`

@ref s 63A(1) (src:6534-6537)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 63A act`
`s 63A(1) a public company must lodge the return of allotments within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 63A(1) lodge with the Registrar a return of the allotments`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not lodge a return of the allotments within 14 days after the allotment"

-- (2) A return of allotment by a public company the shares of which are listed on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore need not state the particulars specified in (1)(e).
-- "listed on an approved exchange in Singapore" is the keel's s 4(1) "listed".
-- src:6573 | (2) A return of allotment mentioned in subsection (1) by a public
-- src:6574 | company, the shares of which are listed on an approved exchange in
-- src:6575 | Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore, need not
-- src:6576 | state the particulars specified in subsection (1)(e).
@ref s 63A(2) (src:6573-6576)
GIVEN `the company has been admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has been removed from that official list` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares of the company are listed on a securities exchange outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63A(2) the return need not state the particulars in subsection (1)(e)` MEANS
    IF    (`s 4(1) "listed" the company or corporation is listed` `the company has been admitted to the official list of an approved exchange in Singapore` `the company has been removed from that official list` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       OR `the shares of the company are listed on a securities exchange outside Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the shares of which are listed on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore, need not state the particulars" -- an unlisted company is not covered by this relief

-- (3) If default is made in complying with this section, every officer of the public company who is in default is guilty of an offence: a fine not exceeding $4,000 and a default penalty of $250.
-- src:6580 | (3) If default is made in complying with this section, every officer
-- src:6581 | of the public company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence
-- src:6582 | and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $4,000 and to
-- src:6583 | a default penalty of $250.
@ref s 63A(3) (src:6580-6583)
DECLARE `s 63A(3) penalty` HAS
    `s 63A(3) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 63A(3) the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `s 63A(3) the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 63A(3) a default penalty is also payable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 63A(3) the default penalty, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
@ref s 63A(3) (src:6580-6583)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 63A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the public company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63A(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    `default is made in complying with section 63A`
      AND `the person is an officer of the public company who is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "If default is made in complying with this section, every officer of the public company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts; it does not say the person is innocent of any other offence
@ref s 63A(3) (src:6580-6583)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 63A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the public company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 63A(3) penalty`
`s 63A(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 63A(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with section 63A` `the person is an officer of the public company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 63A(3) penalty` OF 4000, 0, FALSE, TRUE, 250)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty


§ `Section 63B: lodgment of documents in relation to allotment`

-- 63B.-(1) Where shares are allotted as fully or partly paid up otherwise than in cash and the allotment is made pursuant to a contract in writing, the company must lodge with the return of allotment the contract
-- evidencing the entitlement of the allottee or a copy of any such contract certified as prescribed.
-- src:6589 | 63B.—(1) Where shares are allotted by a company as fully or partly
-- src:6590 | paid up otherwise than in cash and the allotment is made pursuant to a
-- src:6591 | contract in writing, the company must lodge with the return of
-- src:6592 | allotment the contract evidencing the entitlement of the allottee or a
-- src:6593 | copy of any such contract certified as prescribed.
@ref s 63B(1) (src:6589-6593)
GIVEN `the shares are allotted as fully or partly paid up otherwise than in cash` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allotment is made pursuant to a contract in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has lodged with the return of allotment the contract evidencing the entitlement of the allottee, or a copy of it certified as prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63B(1) the company is in default of the duty to lodge the contract with the return of allotment` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the shares are allotted as fully or partly paid up otherwise than in cash` AND `the allotment is made pursuant to a contract in writing`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where shares are allotted by a company as fully or partly paid up otherwise than in cash and the allotment is made pursuant to a contract in writing, the company must lodge" -- a failed "where" (periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a)): the duty does not arise
    ELSE (IF `the company has lodged with the return of allotment the contract evidencing the entitlement of the allottee, or a copy of it certified as prescribed`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must lodge with the return of allotment the contract evidencing the entitlement of the allottee or a copy of any such contract certified as prescribed" -- the duty is done
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

DECLARE `s 63B(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 63B(1) lodge with the return of allotment the contract, or a copy of it certified as prescribed`

-- The duty has no time limit of its own: it is done "with the return of allotment" (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path (sga1)").
@ref s 63B(1) (src:6589-6593)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 63B(1) act`
`s 63B(1) a company must lodge the contract with the return of allotment` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 63B(1) lodge with the return of allotment the contract, or a copy of it certified as prescribed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 63B(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not lodge the contract with the return of allotment" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- (2) If a certified copy of a contract is lodged, the original contract duly stamped must, if the Registrar so requests, be produced at the same time to the Registrar.
-- src:6597 | (2) If a certified copy of a contract is lodged, the original contract
-- src:6598 | duly stamped must if the Registrar so requests be produced at the
-- src:6599 | same time to the Registrar.
@ref s 63B(2) (src:6597-6599)
GIVEN `a certified copy of the contract is lodged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar requests the original contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the original contract duly stamped is produced to the Registrar at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63B(2) the company is in default of the duty to produce the original contract duly stamped` MEANS
    IF `a certified copy of the contract is lodged` AND `the Registrar requests the original contract`
    THEN (IF `the original contract duly stamped is produced to the Registrar at the same time`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the original contract duly stamped must if the Registrar so requests be produced at the same time to the Registrar" -- the duty is done
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a certified copy of a contract is lodged, the original contract duly stamped must if the Registrar so requests be produced" -- a failed "if": no certified copy is lodged, or the Registrar does not request the original (marginal reading (a))

-- (3) Where shares are allotted as fully or partly paid up otherwise than in cash and the allotment is made (a) pursuant to a contract not reduced to writing; (b) pursuant to a provision in the constitution; or (c) in satisfaction
-- of a dividend declared in favour of, but not payable in cash to, the shareholders, or in pursuance of the application of moneys held in an account or reserve in paying up unissued shares to which the shareholders have become
-- entitled, the company must lodge with the Registrar the document specified in (4) within the time specified in (5). (5) The company must lodge the document at the same time and together with the return of allotment.
-- src:6603 | (3) Where shares are allotted as fully or partly paid up otherwise
-- src:6604 | than in cash and the allotment is made —
-- src:6609 | (a) pursuant to a contract not reduced to writing;
-- src:6611 | (b) pursuant to a provision in the constitution; or
-- src:6613 | (c) in satisfaction of a dividend declared in favour of, but not
-- src:6614 | payable in cash to, the shareholders, or in pursuance of the
-- src:6615 | application of moneys held by the company in an account
-- src:6616 | or reserve in paying up unissued shares to which the
-- src:6617 | shareholders have become entitled,
-- src:6619 | the company must lodge with the Registrar the document specified in
-- src:6620 | subsection (4) within the time specified in subsection (5).
@ref s 63B(3) (src:6603-6620)
GIVEN `the shares are allotted as fully or partly paid up otherwise than in cash` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allotment is made pursuant to a contract not reduced to writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allotment is made pursuant to a provision in the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allotment is made in satisfaction of a dividend declared in favour of, but not payable in cash to, the shareholders, or in pursuance of the application of moneys held in an account or reserve in paying up unissued shares to which the shareholders have become entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has lodged the document specified in subsection (4) within the time specified in subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63B(3) the company is in default of the duty to lodge the document specified in subsection (4) with the return of allotment` MEANS
    IF NOT (    `the shares are allotted as fully or partly paid up otherwise than in cash`
            AND (   `the allotment is made pursuant to a contract not reduced to writing`
                 OR `the allotment is made pursuant to a provision in the constitution`
                 OR `the allotment is made in satisfaction of a dividend declared in favour of, but not payable in cash to, the shareholders, or in pursuance of the application of moneys held in an account or reserve in paying up unissued shares to which the shareholders have become entitled`))
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where shares are allotted as fully or partly paid up otherwise than in cash and the allotment is made -- (a) pursuant to a contract not reduced to writing; (b) pursuant to a provision in the constitution; or (c) in satisfaction of a dividend ..., the company must lodge with the Registrar the document specified in subsection (4)" -- a failed "where" (periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a)): the duty does not arise
    ELSE (IF `the company has lodged the document specified in subsection (4) within the time specified in subsection (5)`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must lodge with the Registrar the document specified in subsection (4) within the time specified in subsection (5)" -- the duty is done
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

DECLARE `s 63B(3) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 63B(3) lodge with the return of allotment the document specified in subsection (4)`

-- The time of subsection (5) is "at the same time and together with the return of allotment": the duty has no time limit of its own (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path (sga1)").
@ref s 63B(3) (src:6603-6620)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 63B(3) act`
`s 63B(3) a company must lodge the document specified in subsection (4) with the return of allotment` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 63B(3) lodge with the return of allotment the document specified in subsection (4)`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 63B(3) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not lodge the document specified in subsection (4) with the return of allotment" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- (4) The document referred to in (3) is (a) a statement of prescribed particulars; or (b) in lieu of the statement, where the shares are allotted pursuant to a scheme of arrangement approved by the Court under section 210,
-- a copy of the order of the Court.
DECLARE `s 63B(4) document` IS ONE OF
    `s 63B(4)(a) a statement of prescribed particulars`
    `s 63B(4)(b) a copy of the order of the Court`

-- src:6624 | (4) The document referred to in subsection (3) is —
-- src:6626 | (a) a statement of prescribed particulars; or
-- src:6628 | (b) in lieu of the statement, where the shares are allotted
-- src:6629 | pursuant to a scheme of arrangement approved by the
-- src:6630 | Court under section 210, a copy of the order of the Court.
@ref s 63B(4) (src:6624-6630)
GIVEN `the shares are allotted pursuant to a scheme of arrangement approved by the Court under section 210` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 63B(4) document`
`s 63B(4) the document the company must lodge` MEANS
    IF `the shares are allotted pursuant to a scheme of arrangement approved by the Court under section 210`
    THEN `s 63B(4)(b) a copy of the order of the Court`
    ELSE `s 63B(4)(a) a statement of prescribed particulars`

-- (5) The company must lodge the document specified in (4) at the same time and together with the return of allotment.
-- src:6634 | (5) The company must lodge the document specified in
-- src:6635 | subsection (4) at the same time and together with the return of
-- src:6636 | allotment.
@ref s 63B(5) (src:6634-6636)
GIVEN `the company has lodged the document specified in subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has lodged the return of allotment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document specified in subsection (4) was lodged at the same time as the return of allotment and together with it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63B(5) the document specified in subsection (4) was lodged within the time` MEANS
    IF    `the company has lodged the document specified in subsection (4)`
      AND `the company has lodged the return of allotment`
      AND `the document specified in subsection (4) was lodged at the same time as the return of allotment and together with it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must lodge the document specified in subsection (4) at the same time and together with the return of allotment" (the time the text fixes; the duty's own question)

-- (6) If default is made in complying with this section, every officer of a company who is in default shall each be guilty of an offence: a fine not exceeding $4,000 and a default penalty of $250.
-- src:6640 | (6) If default is made in complying with this section, every officer
-- src:6641 | of a company who is in default shall each be guilty of an offence and
-- src:6642 | shall each be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $4,000 and
-- src:6643 | to a default penalty of $250.
@ref s 63B(6) (src:6640-6643)
DECLARE `s 63B(6) penalty` HAS
    `s 63B(6) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 63B(6) the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `s 63B(6) the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 63B(6) a default penalty is also payable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 63B(6) the default penalty, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
@ref s 63B(6) (src:6640-6643)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 63B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63B(6) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    `default is made in complying with section 63B`
      AND `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "If default is made in complying with this section, every officer of a company who is in default shall each be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts; it does not say the person is innocent of any other offence
@ref s 63B(6) (src:6640-6643)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 63B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 63B(6) penalty`
`s 63B(6) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 63B(6) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with section 63B` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 63B(6) penalty` OF 4000, 0, FALSE, TRUE, 250)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty


§ `Section 63C: notice of increase in total amount paid up on shares`

-- 63C. Where a private company issues any partly paid or unpaid share of any class and the company subsequently receives all or any part of the unpaid amount with respect to the share, the company must lodge with
-- the Registrar a notice in the prescribed form with respect to the total amount of such payments and the increase in the total amount paid up on the relevant class of shares within 14 days after the payment.
-- src:6649 | 63C. Where a private company issues any partly paid or unpaid
-- src:6650 | share of any class and the company subsequently receives all or any
-- src:6651 | part of the unpaid amount with respect to the share, the company must
-- src:6652 | lodge with the Registrar a notice in the prescribed form with respect
-- src:6653 | to the total amount of such payments and the increase in the total
-- src:6654 | amount paid up on the relevant class of shares within 14 days after the
-- src:6655 | payment.
@ref s 63C (src:6649-6655)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company issued a partly paid or unpaid share of a class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company subsequently received all or any part of the unpaid amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the payment was received` IS A DATE
      `the notice has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63C the private company is late in lodging the notice of the increase in the total amount paid up` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company is a private company` AND `the company issued a partly paid or unpaid share of a class` AND `the company subsequently received all or any part of the unpaid amount`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a private company issues any partly paid or unpaid share of any class and the company subsequently receives all or any part of the unpaid amount with respect to the share, the company must lodge" -- a failed "where" (periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a)): the duty does not arise
    ELSE (IF `the notice has been lodged with the Registrar`
          THEN (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the payment was received` `the day the notice was lodged` 14 Days
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must lodge with the Registrar a notice ... within 14 days after the payment" -- lodged within the 14 days (periods ruling (a))
                ELSE JUST TRUE)
          ELSE (IF `the day on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the payment was received` 14 Days
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after the payment" -- the 14 days have not yet run out (periods ruling (a))

DECLARE `s 63C act` IS ONE OF
    `s 63C lodge with the Registrar a notice of the increase in the total amount paid up`

@ref s 63C (src:6649-6655)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 63C act`
`s 63C a private company must lodge the notice of the increase within 14 days after the payment` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 63C lodge with the Registrar a notice of the increase in the total amount paid up`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not lodge the notice of the increase in the total amount paid up within 14 days after the payment"
